WEBVTT

00:30.061 --> 00:34.031
(Azure Spring)

00:34.032 --> 00:36.800
(All characters, places, events, etc. depicted are fictional.)

00:36.801 --> 00:38.970
(Children and animals were filmed under strict guidelines.)

00:50.448 --> 00:54.920
(The 7th Tongyeong Open Water Swimming Competition)

00:58.390 --> 01:00.859
(Tongyeong, Bijin-do, Maemul-do)

01:02.194 --> 01:04.596
What can I do to help him?

01:15.473 --> 01:16.774
(Enjoy the clear sea at Haedam-do, Tongyeong)

01:16.775 --> 01:18.542
(The 7th Tongyeong Open Water Swimming Competition)

01:18.543 --> 01:19.611
Open water swimming?

01:30.422 --> 01:36.428
(Episode 6: Azure Spring)

01:36.962 --> 01:40.297
(7th Tongyeong Open Water Swimming Competition)

01:40.298 --> 01:41.466
Let's compete in a swim meet.

01:45.470 --> 01:46.872
What are you suddenly talking about?

01:48.306 --> 01:50.274
I came to say that to you,

01:50.275 --> 01:51.610
and now that I have, I'm leaving.

01:52.210 --> 01:54.312
How long will you stay underwater?

01:56.147 --> 01:58.250
You told me I had to let things go and come back up...

02:00.385 --> 02:01.620
to live.

02:13.164 --> 02:14.466
I'll teach you...

02:16.468 --> 02:17.669
how to float on water.

02:25.911 --> 02:26.912
Come on.

02:28.013 --> 02:29.147
Hurry up.

02:33.985 --> 02:35.053
Remember the rules?

02:35.453 --> 02:37.154
You get the inner room, and I get the master bedroom.

02:37.155 --> 02:39.156
We share the kitchen and restroom, but we must wash our own dishes.

02:39.157 --> 02:40.792
Why are you doing this to me?

02:42.427 --> 02:43.661
It's just...

02:43.662 --> 02:46.831
kind of scary to see a tanned guy like you with a frown.

02:50.202 --> 02:52.103
I want to make you smile.

03:00.979 --> 03:03.315
Gosh, I'm starving. Why don't we...

03:03.849 --> 03:04.950
eat something first?

03:13.992 --> 03:17.062
Food must be frozen to preserve it longer.

03:50.562 --> 03:52.429
But if you freeze it for too long,

03:52.430 --> 03:53.999
thawing becomes difficult.

04:47.252 --> 04:49.387
What are you waiting for? Come on.

05:15.146 --> 05:17.148
And now, high-five!

05:18.283 --> 05:19.751
The same goes for people's hearts.

05:20.418 --> 05:21.953
A heart left alone for a long time...

05:22.787 --> 05:24.356
doesn't thaw too easily.

05:43.175 --> 05:45.810
That's when you need a special prescription.

06:33.658 --> 06:34.659
Ta-da.

06:35.527 --> 06:37.429
Why don't you take a bite?

06:41.900 --> 06:44.002
Thank you for the food.

07:05.357 --> 07:06.525
Who could've made this?

07:07.058 --> 07:08.560
It's so good!

07:17.903 --> 07:19.371
Here, try this one, too.

07:34.119 --> 07:35.820
- Is it good? - Yes.

07:37.556 --> 07:38.990
Come on. Eat up.

07:56.141 --> 07:57.309
That was delicious.

08:09.187 --> 08:12.190
Since when did you like cats?

08:17.662 --> 08:19.030
I don't particularly like them.

08:20.765 --> 08:22.367
Ever since I came to this island,

08:22.968 --> 08:25.837
I noticed them lingering around, so I've simply been feeding it.

08:28.807 --> 08:33.111
People usually call that liking something.

08:34.746 --> 08:37.215
- Is that so? - Yes.

08:38.149 --> 08:40.384
Who would feed anyone that they hate?

08:40.385 --> 08:41.820
It takes affection.

08:48.727 --> 08:50.128
But that doesn't necessarily mean...

08:50.629 --> 08:52.998
that I like you.

08:57.135 --> 08:58.136
I know.

08:59.171 --> 09:00.805
You wouldn't like a guy like me.

09:02.908 --> 09:04.309
What's so bad about you?

09:04.943 --> 09:08.046
You're perfectly healthy, and you make a living for yourself.

09:08.847 --> 09:09.848
That's enough.

09:13.385 --> 09:15.187
I'm an ex-convict.

09:17.556 --> 09:19.257
I'm aware of that.

09:26.932 --> 09:27.999
I ruined...

09:30.368 --> 09:32.204
two people's lives.

09:37.709 --> 09:40.612
I'm aware of that, too.

09:43.782 --> 09:45.717
That stalker of yours...

09:47.118 --> 09:48.753
came to my place in Seoul.

09:52.157 --> 09:53.158
He asked me...

09:54.459 --> 09:55.927
to save you.

09:57.896 --> 09:59.965
He said you smiled when you were with me.

10:18.416 --> 10:20.051
He was a junior soldier I cared about.

10:23.655 --> 10:27.759
He was soft-hearted, so he wasn't fit to serve in the army.

10:33.465 --> 10:34.666
Like how it always is,

10:36.468 --> 10:38.236
the weak became prey.

10:41.540 --> 10:42.807
He began to get bullied.

10:46.745 --> 10:48.813
And I couldn't tolerate it at that moment.

10:52.617 --> 10:53.985
One died,

10:56.588 --> 10:57.789
and the other...

11:00.625 --> 11:02.327
lives as if he were dead.

11:09.601 --> 11:10.969
At times, I begin to wonder,

11:16.708 --> 11:17.843
"What if..."

11:20.111 --> 11:21.479
"I did not stop him back then?"

11:26.651 --> 11:28.220
It could've ended...

11:31.890 --> 11:34.893
as a simple beating with a broken bone,

11:37.162 --> 11:39.831
and it would've been over.

11:48.273 --> 11:49.274
Then...

11:53.879 --> 11:55.680
that jerk, Nam Sang Ho, would've lived,

12:02.187 --> 12:04.055
and Jae Hui would've been fine, too.

12:18.236 --> 12:19.237
No.

12:23.175 --> 12:25.410
It wouldn't have ended that easily.

12:28.146 --> 12:30.215
The situation would've escalated,

12:33.451 --> 12:34.719
so in the end,

12:38.390 --> 12:39.858
it would've ended in the same way.

12:44.296 --> 12:46.064
You did the right thing.

12:49.401 --> 12:50.869
Everything that happened after that...

12:54.472 --> 12:55.807
is just an accident.

13:06.051 --> 13:07.552
I'm saying...

13:10.555 --> 13:11.623
it wasn't your fault.

13:55.367 --> 13:56.835
I became quite nosy,

13:57.669 --> 13:58.837
thanks to this guy.

14:09.114 --> 14:12.483
Shouldn't the newcomer hand out rice cakes?

14:12.484 --> 14:13.552
Why am I bringing this?

14:14.386 --> 14:16.688
Hey, An Na. My dad told me to give you some rice cake.

14:23.128 --> 14:24.396
Su Jeong?

14:24.829 --> 14:27.299
Seo An Na, you...

14:35.473 --> 14:39.244
Su Jeong, it's not like what it seems.

14:40.212 --> 14:42.646
We ate dinner and talked, then got too exhausted...

14:42.647 --> 14:44.382
How can you do this to me?

14:58.730 --> 14:59.731
Hey!

15:07.405 --> 15:09.373
Hey, look at this.

15:09.374 --> 15:11.008
(7th Tongyeong Open Water Swimming Competition)

15:11.009 --> 15:12.844
We were really talking about the swim meet.

15:14.546 --> 15:16.213
She's right. The swim meet.

15:16.214 --> 15:18.250
She suggested that we compete in this.

15:19.084 --> 15:21.753
You two returned to Parang-ri at the same time on the same day.

15:22.287 --> 15:24.456
Are you saying you talked about the swim meet all night?

15:25.891 --> 15:27.058
But why?

15:27.425 --> 15:29.928
I'm going to settle down here,

15:30.695 --> 15:32.697
so I need to make a living for myself.

15:33.231 --> 15:35.734
I wanted to win the cash prize.

15:36.067 --> 15:37.269
Fine, that's your story.

15:38.303 --> 15:40.739
Why are you competing, Duk Hyun?

15:40.906 --> 15:42.073
I'm not...

15:43.909 --> 15:46.778
I am competing with An Na. Yes.

15:51.883 --> 15:53.151
Then I want to do it, too.

15:53.818 --> 15:56.521
I can't let you two train alone, like you did when harvesting seafood.

15:58.657 --> 16:00.559
Sure. Okay.

16:01.126 --> 16:04.061
You're more than welcome. Yes.

16:04.062 --> 16:05.230
Then I'm in, too.

16:06.831 --> 16:10.402
Why is that new guy back in this backwater village?

16:10.936 --> 16:14.439
That guy paid a dear friend's hospital bill in full.

16:15.006 --> 16:17.142
I want to win the cash prize and pay for half of it.

16:18.109 --> 16:19.945
- Will you let me join? - Yes.

16:20.779 --> 16:21.847
No!

16:24.416 --> 16:25.649
I am...

16:25.650 --> 16:27.185
the Piranha of the Black Snake Unit.

16:27.586 --> 16:28.920
I don't know about everything else,

16:29.287 --> 16:30.856
but I do know I can swim.

16:37.796 --> 16:39.497
The chance of us winning just dropped.

16:47.839 --> 16:49.440
(7th Tongyeong Open Water Swimming Competition)

16:49.441 --> 16:52.943
(Saturday, September 6th, 2025, Tongyeong Haedamdo Beach)

16:52.944 --> 16:55.813
(7th Tongyeong Open Water Swimming Competition)

16:55.814 --> 16:57.781
- Let's go. - It's so pretty. Let's go.

16:57.782 --> 16:59.784
(Sign-Up Form, Seo An Na, 5-1 Parang-ri-gil)

17:08.793 --> 17:10.027
(Name: Yoon Duk Hyun)

17:10.028 --> 17:11.029
(Address)

17:22.474 --> 17:23.875
(Address: 5-1 Parang-ri-gil)

17:33.718 --> 17:36.788
(T-Shirt Size: XL, Signature)

17:44.930 --> 17:46.064
So...

17:47.532 --> 17:51.203
why in the world are you trying to teach me how to swim?

17:54.873 --> 17:56.775
If you ask why it had to be swimming...

18:02.914 --> 18:06.084
All right. Think of the tissue paper as water.

18:06.718 --> 18:09.086
Faster! Do not drop it.

18:09.087 --> 18:11.323
- Pick it up. - It was about the time he'd spend learning.

18:12.023 --> 18:13.859
- I wanted to gift him that moment. - Faster!

18:14.860 --> 18:16.127
- One, two! - One, two!

18:16.695 --> 18:18.129
- One, two! - One, two!

18:18.630 --> 18:19.865
One, two!

18:20.565 --> 18:21.566
One, two!

18:22.467 --> 18:25.237
One, two! Do not drop your shoulders!

18:27.138 --> 18:28.206
One, two!

18:29.941 --> 18:31.910
Just like when he taught me how to harvest seafood.

18:32.978 --> 18:33.979
Good job!

18:34.212 --> 18:35.580
In that moment,

18:36.615 --> 18:38.717
- nothing else was on my mind. - Faster!

18:44.656 --> 18:47.826
I wanted to return that peace to him.

18:56.902 --> 18:59.070
Gosh, I'm starving.

18:59.437 --> 19:02.173
Since we spent time in the water, why don't we eat hot soup?

19:02.174 --> 19:04.009
Your face will get bloated if you have soup at night.

19:04.142 --> 19:06.610
Then what do you eat at night, new guy?

19:06.611 --> 19:09.214
- Me? Salad. - Right. Sure.

19:10.315 --> 19:13.250
Duk Hyun, what do you want to eat?

19:13.251 --> 19:15.020
Anything is fine with me.

19:16.354 --> 19:17.689
So boring.

19:18.790 --> 19:19.991
Okay, I got it.

19:20.759 --> 19:22.694
Hot soup, salad,

19:23.061 --> 19:24.095
and anything.

19:24.462 --> 19:26.231
Let's eat something we'll all be pleased with.

19:59.865 --> 20:00.998
Oh, gosh.

20:00.999 --> 20:04.035
Manila clams are salty, so our faces will definitely get puffy.

20:07.506 --> 20:08.573
Darn it.

21:05.397 --> 21:06.598
Come on.

21:07.065 --> 21:09.601
Seasoned veggies aren't filling enough.

21:12.204 --> 21:13.205
Scoot over.

21:14.105 --> 21:15.373
You're so slow.

21:19.778 --> 21:20.912
You know how to do that?

21:21.479 --> 21:23.882
I was the Frying Pan of the Black Snake Unit.

21:25.917 --> 21:26.918
Not bad.

22:05.824 --> 22:06.825
Here.

22:08.026 --> 22:09.194
Goodness, no way.

22:10.362 --> 22:11.363
What is this?

22:12.597 --> 22:13.598
Is it dog food?

22:14.032 --> 22:15.634
How dare you? "Dog food"?

22:15.967 --> 22:17.269
It's mixed wild green rice.

22:17.669 --> 22:20.539
You're right. Mixed wild green rice is way better than salad.

22:24.209 --> 22:26.711
You just threw in everything you had at home.

22:27.812 --> 22:29.147
Why don't we talk after you try it?

22:35.987 --> 22:38.289
Now, mix. Go!

22:38.290 --> 22:39.291
Go!

22:44.229 --> 22:45.230
Go.

22:49.134 --> 22:50.969
If we continue to learn and mingle together,

22:52.370 --> 22:53.605
the dishes,

22:54.973 --> 22:55.974
the people,

22:57.709 --> 22:58.810
and even wounds...

23:00.145 --> 23:02.848
may start to soften and fade.

23:08.386 --> 23:10.255
It's so good. Hurry up and try it.

23:11.022 --> 23:14.092
It may even get a little better.

23:15.360 --> 23:17.362
Open up, Duk Hyun.

23:17.562 --> 23:18.563
Or not.

23:28.173 --> 23:29.908
Hurry up and try it. It's really good.

24:02.741 --> 24:04.242
It's not so bad for dog food.

24:05.577 --> 24:06.912
Stop calling it dog food.

24:07.479 --> 24:09.047
You liked it, so you can't call it that!

24:17.422 --> 24:18.423
Look.

24:19.157 --> 24:20.458
It's good, though.

24:25.230 --> 24:26.331
Seo An Na.

24:27.098 --> 24:30.000
How dare you dump me and date a guy like that?

24:30.001 --> 24:31.269
That's basically it.

24:37.676 --> 24:39.978
Yoon Duk Hyun!

24:45.517 --> 24:46.518
Yoon Duk Hyun!

24:47.786 --> 24:48.787
Come on out!

24:49.321 --> 24:50.655
Are you here, Yoon Duk Hyun?

24:58.163 --> 25:00.865
Chief, what brings you here?

25:00.866 --> 25:02.234
Baek Su Jeong, you brat.

25:02.701 --> 25:05.237
Why did you sleep here instead of your own home?

25:06.338 --> 25:07.638
Come on, Dad.

25:07.639 --> 25:09.640
I'm old enough, so don't nag at me for spending the night out...

25:09.641 --> 25:10.941
on this tiny little island.

25:10.942 --> 25:12.644
Well, no. It's not that.

25:13.278 --> 25:14.679
Doesn't Yoon Duk Hyun live here?

25:15.580 --> 25:17.715
What about him?

25:17.716 --> 25:19.317
It's not like he just moved in.

25:19.584 --> 25:20.585
That kid is...

25:22.320 --> 25:23.321
Look.

25:24.322 --> 25:26.358
- There he is. - What's going on?

25:26.925 --> 25:29.861
I thought you had left the island. Why did you return?

25:31.162 --> 25:34.032
Did I cause an inconvenience with my return?

25:34.366 --> 25:35.433
Of course, you have!

25:36.701 --> 25:38.904
We all know who you are now.

25:40.672 --> 25:41.907
Dad.

25:42.807 --> 25:44.109
What do you mean?

25:45.677 --> 25:46.845
Who is he?

25:50.348 --> 25:53.084
That he's a murderer who killed a person.

25:54.753 --> 25:55.787
Cha Jae Hun.

25:57.522 --> 26:00.025
An Na, you... Gosh.

26:00.926 --> 26:04.429
Wait, have you been hitting it off with him, knowing who he is?

26:05.163 --> 26:07.666
An Na, what's he talking about?

26:08.867 --> 26:12.070
Did Duk Hyun kill a person?

26:13.238 --> 26:16.474
One died, and the other is a vegetable.

26:17.008 --> 26:18.610
Technically, he killed two people.

26:22.781 --> 26:24.282
Excuse me, Chief.

26:24.716 --> 26:27.918
How can you let a guy like that stay in this peaceful village?

26:27.919 --> 26:29.688
Jae Hun, how dare you?

26:47.672 --> 26:48.673
I'm sorry.

26:50.442 --> 26:51.877
I couldn't bring myself to tell you.

26:53.712 --> 26:54.713
I will leave the island...

26:55.547 --> 26:56.648
within the day.

26:57.983 --> 26:58.984
Yes!

26:59.951 --> 27:01.620
You should've said that in the first place.

27:07.626 --> 27:08.960
You should've told us...

27:10.495 --> 27:12.998
when you got here three years ago.

27:25.510 --> 27:26.811
Keeping that all to yourself...

27:28.380 --> 27:29.514
must've been tough.

27:36.254 --> 27:37.255
I bet.

27:38.023 --> 27:40.158
We've known you for a long time.

27:40.492 --> 27:43.328
He lived all three years just harvesting seafood.

27:44.896 --> 27:47.065
We all know how to use the Internet.

27:47.699 --> 27:50.335
We already looked into the details of the incident.

27:50.869 --> 27:53.271
- You went through a lot. - It must've been tough.

27:56.541 --> 27:58.944
What are these old people saying?

27:59.845 --> 28:02.147
This punk killed a person!

28:04.749 --> 28:05.884
Darn it.

28:07.052 --> 28:08.420
Hey, An Na. Come on out.

28:09.821 --> 28:10.856
- An Na! - Hey!

28:14.726 --> 28:15.727
Let go.

28:16.027 --> 28:17.028
Didn't you hear me?

28:18.029 --> 28:20.999
- I'm a former swimmer. - Is that so?

28:22.367 --> 28:23.702
- I was a judo wrestler. - What?

28:36.047 --> 28:37.381
Only until elementary school.

28:37.382 --> 28:39.518
- My goodness. - You're a strong one!

28:40.085 --> 28:41.086
- Goodness. - Good one.

28:41.486 --> 28:44.756
Anyway, now that you're back,

28:45.056 --> 28:47.559
live a good life here without thinking of running away.

28:47.926 --> 28:50.529
- Got it? - He's right.

28:51.096 --> 28:55.033
A young man like you is rare in this small island village.

28:55.834 --> 28:58.103
- Got it? - That's right!

28:58.403 --> 29:00.172
- There's nothing much to life. - That's true.

29:00.705 --> 29:04.208
Life is about learning how to coexist with others.

29:04.209 --> 29:05.443
He's right.

29:06.878 --> 29:08.113
- Where's the rice cake? - Here.

29:09.080 --> 29:11.148
Where's the rice cake? Bring it here.

29:11.149 --> 29:12.150
Have some rice cake.

29:12.784 --> 29:14.486
Once you've moved to a new place,

29:14.853 --> 29:17.488
it's customary to give out steamed rice cakes.

29:17.489 --> 29:19.357
- He's right. - Open up.

29:19.624 --> 29:21.158
I already gave him some.

29:21.159 --> 29:23.028
That was for An Na.

29:24.529 --> 29:25.864
All of you, open up.

29:27.866 --> 29:28.867
Have some.

29:30.035 --> 29:31.036
Open up.

29:33.638 --> 29:35.240
It's nice to see you eat well.

29:37.275 --> 29:40.712
- Do you want some? - Goodness. Leave them for the kids.

29:43.248 --> 29:44.583
Just as the elders said,

29:45.350 --> 29:48.620
I guess there really isn't much to life.

29:49.387 --> 29:51.989
It's customary to give out rice cakes to the elders...

29:51.990 --> 29:53.391
and visit them when you move in.

29:55.093 --> 29:58.362
Goodness. Stop crying.

29:58.363 --> 30:01.800
You're a grown man. Don't cry. It's all right.

30:02.434 --> 30:04.769
We understand. Goodness.

30:05.604 --> 30:08.640
- Don't cry. - There, there. I'm glad you're here.

30:10.108 --> 30:11.375
Look at this guy.

30:11.376 --> 30:14.479
- Even bottled-up feelings and tangled emotions... - Oh, no. Come on now.

30:15.447 --> 30:19.084
all seem to melt away with a bite of steamed rice cake.

30:33.465 --> 30:35.534
Hey, that's pretty far.

30:36.535 --> 30:37.536
I'm out.

30:38.670 --> 30:41.106
No one told me about Duk Hyun,

30:41.506 --> 30:42.607
so I'm pouting.

30:43.041 --> 30:45.544
Cut it out. We're starting the open-water training from today.

30:46.011 --> 30:48.547
This is the starting point, and the buoy is the turning point.

30:49.381 --> 30:51.116
Dinner's on the loser.

30:51.516 --> 30:52.517
What do you say?

30:53.218 --> 30:54.319
Go!

30:54.653 --> 30:58.556
Hey! It'll cost a fortune to feed four people!

30:58.557 --> 30:59.791
Let's go!

31:01.159 --> 31:02.494
Hey, it's raining.

31:02.827 --> 31:04.228
- What? - Darn it.

31:04.229 --> 31:06.831
- It's raining. - Let's go home.

31:27.519 --> 31:28.687
- Duk Hyun. - Let's go home.

31:29.287 --> 31:31.156
- Come on. - Wait for me!

31:35.360 --> 31:36.361
Hurry.

31:37.462 --> 31:38.597
Jeez.

31:42.400 --> 31:43.635
Hand it over quickly.

31:46.638 --> 31:47.906
Say pretty please.

31:49.040 --> 31:50.041
Darn it.

31:51.376 --> 31:52.844
I'll give it to you.

31:54.513 --> 31:55.714
You're too slow!

31:57.048 --> 31:59.251
I can't do this!

32:02.721 --> 32:05.523
- Hey, don't drop it. - I can't do it!

32:05.524 --> 32:07.192
- I'm not doing this! - Hey!

32:12.764 --> 32:13.865
Come on!

32:19.638 --> 32:22.473
Hello, I signed up for the open-water competition.

32:22.474 --> 32:24.576
By any chance, will it be cancelled tomorrow?

32:25.043 --> 32:27.045
We'll know for sure when tomorrow comes.

32:27.646 --> 32:29.980
But tomorrow is the competition.

32:29.981 --> 32:31.949
The typhoon is moving fast,

32:31.950 --> 32:35.019
so the forecast said we might move out of its path soon.

32:35.020 --> 32:37.155
I see. All right.

32:38.990 --> 32:42.894
No matter how hard we try, we can never predict what's ahead.

32:49.935 --> 32:50.969
All we can do is...

32:51.670 --> 32:53.638
just live the life we're given.

33:03.648 --> 33:05.816
(Tongyeong Open Water Swimming Competition)

33:05.817 --> 33:07.619
(Congratulations on finishing the race.)

33:17.162 --> 33:18.597
With all these set up,

33:19.164 --> 33:21.867
I guess the competition will carry on as planned, right?

33:22.234 --> 33:23.835
The weather cleared up, too.

33:24.503 --> 33:27.205
- I'm sure it'll happen. - No, I don't think so.

33:27.606 --> 33:29.374
We have an announcement.

33:29.474 --> 33:32.009
The open-water swimming competition scheduled for today...

33:32.010 --> 33:33.978
has been cancelled...

33:33.979 --> 33:37.749
due to safety concerns caused by strong currents in the high seas.

33:38.049 --> 33:40.784
The entry fee will be fully refunded.

33:40.785 --> 33:44.990
We thank you once again for coming out today.

33:45.590 --> 33:47.092
Yes! I got it right!

33:47.459 --> 33:48.793
Why are you happy about that?

33:49.194 --> 33:50.862
We trained so hard!

33:51.897 --> 33:54.299
What now, Duk Hyun?

33:54.833 --> 33:57.234
We can't help it. Let's go back.

33:57.235 --> 33:58.236
No.

33:59.004 --> 34:01.573
We came all the way here, so it's a huge bummer.

34:02.741 --> 34:04.209
Let's do the competition...

34:05.544 --> 34:06.811
- on our own. - What?

34:07.746 --> 34:08.747
On our own?

34:09.314 --> 34:12.816
We have the participants, the swimsuits, and the sea.

34:12.817 --> 34:15.153
- Why not? - They said it was dangerous.

34:15.587 --> 34:17.355
We'll only go out to the safe area.

34:18.256 --> 34:19.324
How about up to that buoy?

34:19.991 --> 34:22.360
To that buoy?

34:24.930 --> 34:26.331
All right, now.

34:27.065 --> 34:31.770
Let us begin the first Parang-ri Swimming Competition!

34:32.137 --> 34:34.739
The loser has to do the dishes for a month.

34:34.840 --> 34:36.808
Ready, go!

34:37.108 --> 34:40.879
Jeez, she's being so childish again.

34:44.282 --> 34:46.785
But I won't lose against you... Hey!

34:47.185 --> 34:50.255
Hey, wait! This isn't fair!

35:30.328 --> 35:32.797
Just like the weather at sea,

35:33.265 --> 35:34.933
life is unpredictable.

35:38.336 --> 35:41.173
Maybe that's why we just have to go with the flow,

35:41.606 --> 35:43.475
like we're being swept away by the waves.

35:47.279 --> 35:50.348
But it's okay to live like that.

35:56.588 --> 35:58.256
Just do what you can,

35:59.658 --> 36:02.194
as much as you can, and live on.

36:27.352 --> 36:29.120
Youth isn't momentary,

36:29.855 --> 36:30.956
but lasts a lifetime.

36:33.225 --> 36:37.028
Because for us, today will always be spring and azure.

36:44.135 --> 36:45.570
- May it last a long time. - May it last a long time.

36:46.271 --> 36:48.173
- Azure spring. - Azure spring.

36:50.475 --> 36:56.481
(Azure Spring)

37:09.261 --> 37:10.495
Come here! Quickly!

37:12.564 --> 37:14.599
- Come on! - Hurry up, man.

37:15.233 --> 37:16.467
- The timer's about to go off. - Where?

37:16.468 --> 37:17.736
One, two!

37:55.373 --> 38:01.246
(Thank you for watching Azure Spring)
